  "worked_solution": "To compute ${f}^{\u2032}(-2),$ we need to find the slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ at $x=-2.$\n\nLet's consider the graph of $y=f(x)$ for $x\\in [-5,0].$ Notice that $x=-2$ lies in this interval.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934289/assets/2f46cbe001623cacc7e7ae8f54d73f2bbc9ce685a9f75ffa93d78a9c621722fe.png)\n\nThe slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in (-5,-1)$ is constant and equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u0394f}{\u0394x} & =\\frac{-2-3}{-1-(-5)}=\\frac{-5}{4}=-1.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{\u2032}(-2)=-1.25.$",
